TITLE:: SDGMaster
summary:: the master track: everything not sent direct, a mastering chain, a fader, the hardware output
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SDGBusTrack, Classes/SDGGroup, Classes/SDGReturn, Classes/SuperDirtGUI

DESCRIPTION::
Every orbit, group and return writes to the master unless it is sent straight to a
hardware bus, and the master writes to the hardware - where orbit 0 wrote before there
was a master (link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-hardwareOut::). Everything it does is
link::Classes/SDGBusTrack::; it has no sends, mute or solo, and always goes direct.

code::
m = ~sdg.master;
~sdg.addBusInsert(m, \eq);
~sdg.addBusInsert(m, \compressor);
m.level = 0.9;
m.limitertype = 1;                        // a limiter after the fader
::

The link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: makes it once the orbits exist, unless
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#*useMaster:: is false; an orbit that wrote somewhere other
than orbit 0's bus keeps writing there. With no effect and the fader at 0 dB it changes
nothing. link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-free:: takes it out and sends the orbits back to
the hardware.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Made by link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-addMaster::, not by hand.
ARGUMENT:: sdg
the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: shortName
RETURNS:: "master".

METHOD:: route
It only goes direct: the argument is ignored.
ARGUMENT:: argDest
ignored.
ARGUMENT:: bus
the hardware bus; nil keeps the one it has.
